# Source renders that tools/cutout.py consumes. At fs-penalty these stayed
# tracked, 22 MB of them, in a public repo — still downloadable from
# raw.githubusercontent.com long after Pages was cleaned. The art is
# reproducible from the prompts in docs/ART.md, so the blobs never need to be.
raw/

# Placeholder art carried over from fs-penalty so the ported page runs while
# the Top Win art is being made. None of it belongs in this repo's history:
# the keeper wears FanSport's kit, the plate is graded to their green/purple,
# and the ball is painted with their LIME and PURPLE -- the plan had the ball
# down as brand-neutral, and it is not. Etapa 3 replaces all of it and deletes
# this block. The ball is the cheap one: two constants at the top of
# tools/ball_sheet.py and one run of the script.
assets/img/keeper-*.webp
assets/img/pitch-spot.webp
assets/img/ball.webp
assets/img/ball-spin.webp
